			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1700133">
									

<p>In a way, it's more similar to SCP-051. Here's how I see my idea and what makes it unique in my opinion:</p>
<p>If this severe effect of SCP-1816 was just caused randomly, it would be lethal in most cases. What I am trying to convey without saying it explicitely is that the tree may have some form of sentience and is doing it's stuff on purpose. Mrs Z. certainly believes that, but of course the reader is left to imagine whether she is right or not.</p>
<p>My original idea was that the bonsai was doing that out of spite and for revenge. Now I think more that it is doing it for artistic reasons. It's still up to the reader to decide.</p>
<p>It's a story about the relativity of beauty and horror and how one can be at the center of the other. Like Yin and Yang.</p>

